Theorem 27.4 There is a semifan \(\mcf\) such that there exists a morphism \[
\Psi: (\overline{F_\Co})^{
u} 	o \overline{F_\Co}^{\mcf}
\] from the normalization of the KSBA compactification to the semitoroidal compactification associated with \(\mcf\). The Coxeter fan of \(T_{\Co}\) is a refinement of \(\mcf\), and stable Coble surfaces in the boundary of \(\overline{F_\Co}\) admit explicit descriptions in terms of surfaces associated to sub-Dynkin diagrams of Coxeter diagrams.


Remark 27.5 This result is made possible by recent advances in (Alexeev and Engel 2022; Alexeev et al. 2024) on compactifications of K3 surfaces with nonsymplectic automorphisms, along with the theory of recognizable divisors developed in (Alexeev and Engel 2023). We also critically leverage the related stable pair compactification of the moduli spaces of Enriques surfaces studied in (Alexeev et al. 2025). In particular, we use the folding theory of Coxeter diagrams, their associated integral affine structures, and the theory of \(ADE+BC\) surfaces in order to explicitly describe stable degenerations of Coble surfaces.

