The lattices for \(S_{\Nod}\) comes from (Dolgachev and Kondō 2013 Prop. 3.1). There is a primitive embedding
\[
 egin{aligned}
    \sen &\injects S_{\Nod} \
    U(2) \oplus E_{8}(2) &\injects U \oplus \generators{-4}  \oplus E_8(2) \
    ( (e, f), x) &\mapsto ( (2	ilde f + 	ilde g + h, 	ilde g), x)
\end{aligned}
\]
where \(U(2) = \generators{e,f}\), \(U = \generators{	ilde e, 	ilde f}\), and \(\generators{-4} = \generators{h}\); this map is the identity on the \(E_8(2)\) component. This formula is given on (Cossec et al. 2025, 561). There it is claimed that this induces a map \(F_{S_{\Nod}} \injects F_{\sen}\) where the former coincides with the moduli space of nodal Enriques surfaces. Geometrically, a nodal Enriques surface is one that contains a smooth rational curve, i.e. a \((-2)\)-curve (Cossec et al. 2025); the embedding above is thus the lattice-theoretic avatar of this locus inside \(F_{\sen}\).
\[
 egin{aligned}
S_{\Nod} &= (11, 10, 1)_1 = \generators{-4} \oplus E_{10}(2) & T_{\Nod} &= (11, 8, 1)_2 \,\,\,= \generators{4} \oplus U \oplus E_8(2)
\end{aligned}
\]




Cossec, François, Igor Dolgachev, and Christian Liedtke. 2025. Enriques Surfaces I. 2nd ed. Springer Nature Singapore. https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-96-1214-7.


Dolgachev, Igor, and Shigeyuki Kondō. 2013. “The Rationality of the Moduli Spaces of Coble Surfaces and of Nodal Enriques Surfaces.” Izvestiya: Mathematics 77.

